{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"Your servants have taken up the head of the men of war who are in our hand\"</b> is as follows: Behold, HaShem wrought a great deliverance through us, in that not one of all the men of the army who were in our hand died in the war, nor was anyone struck by the sword so as to be missing from the army. Therefore we desire to offer an offering to HaShem who delivered us, to present before Him an atonement for our souls, which He redeemed from death and in war from the hand of the sword. And our Sages expounded (Shabbat 64a): \"and there was not missed from us a man\" — to speak of transgression, meaning that at all times they were in our hand and no man from our brethren who were in the army went off to another place to commit a transgression. And Moses said to them: If so, why this offering? They said to him: To atone for our souls from the musings of the heart."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:53.748334701Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}